.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A typed view over a raw \fR\fBCache\fP\fP that exposes elements of an unmanaged type \fIT\fP \&. 

\fRTypeBuffer<T>\fP provides element access, cloning, clearing and simple fill semantics for fixed‑stride unmanaged types\&. The buffer owns an internal \fR\fBCache\fP\fP instance sized to \fRlength * sizeof(T)\fP\&. All reads and writes perform endian conversion using the configured \fBEndian\fP value\&. 

.PP
This type assumes \fIT\fP  is an unmanaged value type and uses a fixed stride equal to \fRsizeof(T)\fP\&. Index and offset parameters are validated by the underlying cache and may throw on out‑of‑range access\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP An unmanaged value type stored in the buffer\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBType Constraints\fP
.TP
\fIT\fP : \fIunmanaged\fP
